{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series","excerpts":[["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:escape-irrational","exact rationality classification","<p><em>\nFor a real integer-coefficient recurrence, the following are equivalent:\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>; <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span> for some <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>; and, for some fixed <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span> at every sufficiently large\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span>. More precisely, if <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi></msup><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is in lowest terms, with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span> odd, then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>den</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟺</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>s</mi><mtext> </mtext><mtext>and</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mo>∣</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Consequently <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span> is irrational exactly when every\npositive shift is nonintegral at every index, equivalently when for each\nfixed <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> there are arbitrarily\nlate nonintegral shifts.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:gap-nonperiodic","prime gaps do not become periodic","<p><em> For every positive <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi></math></span>, the\nactual consecutive-prime-gap sequence is not eventually periodic with\nperiod <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:infinite","prime-to-gap identity","<p><em> The actual\nprime and gap series satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Π</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>G</mi></math></span>. Their complete tails </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> satisfy\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>. Thus <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Π</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>G</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span> have the same rationality\nstatus.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:irr-equivalence","exact irrationality reformulation","<p><em> The prime-value dyadic series is irrational if and only if the\nprime-gap dyadic series is. Both series converge by the polynomial bound\nproved above; neither side is proved irrational.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:jointcountermodel","a rational sum with the stated\nprime-gap statistics","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo></math></span> be the primes and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>. Given <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, there is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>b</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> with rational dyadic sum such\nthat <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>ε</mi></msup></math></span>\neventually. For every fixed positive modulus, both the coefficients and\nthe cumulative positions eventually retain their corresponding residues.\nThe empirical distributions of unnormalised blocks have total variation\ndistance tending to zero for lengths <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, and for every fixed\nnonzero <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></span>,\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\" fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\" fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nMoreover, with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mspace width=\"-0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> These positions are not asserted to be\nprime.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:signedwindow","two consecutive differences of\nabsolute value less than one","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></math></span>. The conditions <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>δ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> hold exactly when, for some\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> In\nthat case <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> and both\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></math></span> are nonintegral.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:sparserationalisation","sparse changes preserving\ncongruences","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>\nsatisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span>,\nlet <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span>, and let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></math></span> tend to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span>. There exist a set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> of upper Banach\ndensity zero and a nondegenerate interval <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>I</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> such that, for every\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></math></span>, there is an integer\ncorrection <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfying\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>eventually</mtext><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For each integer\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> there is a cutoff <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></math></span>, independent of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi></math></span>, such that <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>q</mi><mo>∣</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math></span> for all <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></math></span>. For every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, the choice <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>ε</mi></msup></math></span> can be made\nwith </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mspace width=\"-0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>∩</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow><mi>X</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> In particular the distance tends\nto zero for every integer-valued <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, uniformly over target\nvalues.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:true-tail","the boundary condition for the tail\nrecurrence","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span> and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math></span>. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> for every\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span> if and only if <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-251-prime-gap-dyadic-series#res:truncation","finite separation criterion","<p><em> If\nfor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and every cutoff\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></span> there are <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> with </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>5</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> then <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Π</mi></math></span> is\nirrational.</em></p>"]]}
